      "title": "Module 2 Conclusion — What Your First Move Taught You",
      "slug": "module-two-conclusion",
      "instructions": "# Module 2 Conclusion\n\nA useful first action is not necessarily one that succeeds. You may have learned from a small attempt, or you may have learned that a barrier needs to be addressed first.\n\nLook at your original First Move Card, the feedback you received and your Launch Portfolio. Which part of your plan is now clearer? What is still uncertain? Choose one next step that makes sense based on the evidence available, not what you wish had happened.\n\nThe same planning questions can help with a different project: Why does it matter? What is manageable now? What could I observe? What would the observation not prove? Who could provide appropriate support?\n\nYou are leaving this course with a process you can reuse, not a requirement to finish a giant project in one sitting.\n\nReview your actual evidence and any facilitator feedback before the closing reflection. No additional graded submission is required here.\n\n### Finish the course\n\nComplete Your Next Move, then use the course navigation to open the Quiz and Evaluation. The quiz checks your knowledge. The ungraded evaluation asks about your experience of the course and is separate from your confidence reflection.",
